Neurologic Solutions Enters into Exclusive License Agreement for Breakthrough Epilepsy Technologies 
[Baltimore, MD] — [August 24, 2026] — Neurologic Solutions today announced an agreement to license technologies developed by Sridevi Sarma, PhD, a researcher from Johns Hopkins University Whiting School of Engineering, to commercialize EZTrackTM and EpiScalpTM, two revolutionary, software-driven technologies aimed at transforming epilepsy diagnosis and surgical treatment.
Developed in Sarma’s laboratory, these advanced algorithmic tools leverage machine learning and brain network modeling to address critical gaps in epilepsy care.
Redefining Epilepsy Diagnosis and Surgery
EpiScalpTM targets the high rate of epilepsy misdiagnosis. By using machine learning to analyze neural network interactions between seizures, it can identify hidden biomarkers in routine, 20-minute scalp EEGs. Recent clinical data shows EpiScalpTM can potentially reduce misdiagnoses by nearly 70%.
EZTrackTM serves as a digital mapmaker for patients requiring surgery. For the millions who do not respond to medication, EZTrackTM processes complex brain data to generate a localized heat map of the exact "epileptogenic zone" where a patient's seizures originate, significantly improving surgical success rates.
"Securing the licenses for EZTrackTM and EpiScalpTM is a major milestone," said Andy Gothsalk, CEO of Neurologic Solutions. "By pairing EpiScalpTM 's early diagnostic precision with EZTrackTM’s surgical mapping, we are establishing an end-to-end suite of tools that will fundamentally change the treatment path for patients with epilepsy."
Neurologic Solutions will now focus on integrating both software applications into existing clinical workflows, advancing regulatory pathways, and establishing partnerships with leading neurological centers.
About Neurologic Solutions Neurologic Solutions is an innovative MedTech startup dedicated to developing cutting-edge digital health software that transforms neurodiagnostic workflows. The company’s flagship platform, EpiScalpTM, provides neurologists with advanced, intelligent software applications to detect, analyze, and assist in the diagnosis of epilepsy and related neurological conditions. Neurologic Solutions aims to drastically improve clinical efficiency and elevate patient care globally.
